  "about": "Who has work to go to (FolkJobs, docs/WORLD_LIFE.md). A spot is a cell; \"facing\" is degrees from north, \"out\" is the land a spot over the water is reached from. A job's people go round its stops for ever: \"stay\" is [least, most] seconds, \"do\" is watch, tend or gesture, and \"night\" keeps them out after dark. The walks between are found over the land, so the road is taken because it's quicker. \"inARun\" is the stop a job's people walk to and keep to while a Hold run is on, off the raiders' road; after it they take up the round again there.",
